# Pick ONE can and place it. Served by cobot_operation (Python choreography),
# which chains cobot_control primitives (MoveToPose, set_output_bit, the
# /cobot/state sensor poll). The layer loop lives in the task manager, which
# sends these goals sequentially.
#
# Cancel policy: IMMEDIATE — the in-flight MoveToPose is canceled (controller
# MotionStop) and the choreography returns at once. The can may still be
# gripped and the arm may be mid-segment; result.phase says where it stopped.
# /cobot/pause on cobot_operation holds the arm in place and blocks the next
# primitive until /cobot/resume.
Target target
---
bool success
string message
string phase                  # phase in which the goal ended
JobResult[] jobs              # every primitive executed, in order
SensorAssert[] sensor_asserts
---
string phase    # check / approach / grip / lift / place — mirrors choreography
